roperty; flood, wind, and earthquake; excess liability or umbrella; general liability, and property and auto insurance for small businesses; life insurance; and motorcycle, recreational vehicle, and other insurance policies. It distributes its products and services through corporate and franchise locations. Goosehead Insurance, Inc. was founded in 2003 and is headquartered in Westlake, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Mark K. Miller CPA | CEO & Director | Age 59 | Compensation: $1.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $228K ranks in the bottom quartile among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 29%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $54K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $15K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Goosehead Insurance, Inc. is a small-cap financial services business with a $1.6B market cap on $365M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +20% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +6.2pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 35% against a 10% cost of capital \u2014 a 25-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $86M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 24 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 3.30\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 3.1\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 13.8% 